       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is double the maximum recommended metformin dose. The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is substantially higher, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals** (1,700 mg/day)\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO** at some other frequency\n- Something else\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
